<del></del></span> Best Arcane Mage Trinkets in Phase 3</span></h2>DPS trinkets tend to be very straightforward, as their damage is not affected by class damage buffs. Therefore, direct damage dealing trinkets should be used on cooldown as much as possible, unless aligned with specific boss damage taken increasing mechanics, and stat increasing trinkets should similarly either be used on cooldown or aligned with burst phases.<br/>
<br/>Additionally, it's relevant to note that soon after Phase 3 releases, the new Celestial Dungeons will become available - and with that the Raid trinkets mentioned here will become available through said Dungeons in their LFR versions, and are solid options over the bottom two trinkets.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96516/cha-yes-essence-of-brilliance">
<img alt="Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_mindsooth.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance</span></a> is Phase 3's best trinket for Arcane Mages, being able to convert a large chunk of its Critical Strike stat into Mastery as well as its solid Intellect proc makes for a very solid item.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96558/unerring-vision-of-lei-shen">
<img alt="Unerring Vision of Lei Shen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_hunter_focusedaim.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unerring Vision of Lei Shen</span></a> is Arcane's second best trinket this phase, given that when combining its high initial proc rate when entering combat, as well as Arcane's somewhat relevant dependency on its initial burst for a large chunk of its total damage, leads this trinket adds to that very well.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96455/breath-of-the-hydra">
<img alt="Breath of the Hydra" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_mindflay.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Breath of the Hydra</span></a> is about 3% weaker than the next best option, but still relevant temporarily if you can obtain it with no strings attached (such as being required to pass one of the best in slot trinkets).</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96413/wushoolays-final-choice">
<img alt="Wushoolay's Final Choice" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_chainlightning.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wushoolay's Final Choice</span></a> performs even worse than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96455/breath-of-the-hydra">
<img alt="Breath of the Hydra" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_mindflay.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Breath of the Hydra</span></a>, but is still an upgrade over last phase's options as well as the current reputation trinket.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94510/volatile-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Volatile Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_hunter_posthaste.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Volatile Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> is available through the new Phase 3 raid reputation (Shado-Pan Assault) and although the reputation is mostly obtainable through Throne of Thunder, you can easily get Friendly without it via content on the Isle of Thunder. This trinket is a great option for people either upgrading from past tier items, as well as for people catching up.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> is, although outscaled, still very relevant for people wanting to catch-up to end-game content quickly, as it's a pretty affordable option that competes with way higher item level trinkets from last phase.</div></li></ul>
