<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Arcane Mages</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 15%. Keep in mind that some abilities such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-expertise-rating">Hit &amp; Expertise Rating</h4>At 15% Hit, your spells will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. It's also relevant to note that Expertise now counts as Hit and should be added together for the total of 15% to reach said cap.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Arcane Mages</span></h2>For Arcane Mage you'll aim to stack as much mastery as possible using gems, so a mix of <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76700/fractured-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Fractured Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Sun's Radiance</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76643/senseis-wild-jade">
<img alt="Sensei's Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sensei's Wild Jade</span></a> depending on the socket type will be the go-to. As for the Red sockets, the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76672/artful-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Artful Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Artful Vermilion Onyx</span></a> provides mastery as well as Intellect making it the best.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95347/sinister-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Sinister Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sinister Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76672/artful-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Artful Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Artful Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c7">Blue Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76643/senseis-wild-jade">
<img alt="Sensei's Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sensei's Wild Jade</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c4">Yellow Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76700/fractured-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Fractured Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Sun's Radiance</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Arcane Mages</span></h2>Every profession is relatively viable in Mists of Pandaria Classic, but engineering is always in somewhat of a class above due to the high quality of life tools it provides and safety net of nitro boosts. Tailoring also continues to be the best profession, especially due to its main ICD benefit being oftentimes re-applied with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=108978/alter-time">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_mage_altertime.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alter Time</span></a>.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Arcane Mages</h4>Engineering has plenty of quality of life tools, such as repair bots, access to the bank in raids, an extra slow fall option and such, but the two main factors that make it so good for PVE are:<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> is an on-demand big main stat cooldown which can then be prolonged with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=108978/alter-time">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_mage_altertime.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alter Time</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a> allows the player to escape mechanics that one would otherwise not be able to get out of, as well as helping correct major mistakes in positioning with far less of a uptime loss.</div></li></ul>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Arcane Mages</h4>The main reason for getting tailoring is <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125481/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a>, this proc provides a fairly large amount of main stat, usually when most of your other cooldowns are also ongoing.<br/>As a bonus, you also get a far cheaper leg enchant with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125496/masters-spellthread">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_astralrecalgroup.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Master's Spellthread</span></a>, since you don't have to buy the enchant from other players.<br/>Lastly, you can craft some BoE and BoP items that are useful at the start of the expansion. These aren't mandatory to obtain, but always nice to have the option to craft them.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Arcane Mages</span></h3>With Phase 3, we now get two new tailoring crafting options that are actually relevant:<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94278/falling-blossom-cowl">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Cowl" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_cloth_raidmage_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Cowl</span></a> - Although, not listed above, this is a great option as an off-piece to use four-piece tier 15 set around assuming you are filling in those gaps with the Celestial versions of the set. At least until you get better items such as the best in slot chestpiece and/<wbr/>or the heroic tier 15 headpiece to replace it directly with.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94277/falling-blossom-treads">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Treads" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_cloth_raidmage_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Treads</span></a> - is a straight upgrade from past phase options and with an additional socket it's great for both regular PVE content, and as Challenge Mode best in slot if you choose to do that later on, meaning your gold isn't wasted once you replace it in your raiding set.</div></li></ul>
